From 14004835f153c3fde6af2a21332490fdde3c6ed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:49:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] xdg_decoration: Adds support for the KDE server
 decoration protocol.

GTK3 does not implement xdg-decoration-unstable-v1, but binds
org_kde_kwin_server_decoration_manager and requests server-side
decorations for windows without a client-side header bar. Without it,
such windows remained undecorated in wlmaker.

Creates the wlr_server_decoration_manager next to the XDG decoration
manager. Its default mode follows the configured `Decoration` `Mode`
(Suggest/EnforceServer: server, Suggest/EnforceClient: client), and each
decoration's mode is applied to the XDG toplevel through the same path as
for XDG decoration, with Enforce* overriding the client's request. If the
decoration is created before the toplevel, it is applied on the first
surface commit that has one.

Adds unit tests for the mode mapping and the decoration lifecycle.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
